<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese two-month car sales fall 4.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese two-month car sales fall 4.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto-Dealers</p>
<p>Association (ACAP) announced the following new cars</p>
<p>registrations:</p>
<p>February 1997 17,509 vs 17,902 (down 2.2 pct)</p>
<p>Jan/Feb  1997 33,478 vs 35,133 (down 4.7 pct)</p>
<p>First two months by manufacturers' markets share (percentage</p>
<p>in brackets). Comparative figures refer to same period 1996:</p>
<p>    Opel	  4,932 (14.73) vs 4,910 (13.98)</p>
<p>    Fiat	  4,717 (14.09) vs 4,958 (14.11)</p>
<p>    Renault     4,416 (13.19) vs 4,841 (13.78)</p>
<p>    Ford	  3,006 (08.98) vs 3,782 (10.76)</p>
<p>    Volkswagen  2,792 (08.34) vs 2,774 (07.90)</p>
<p>    Citroen     2,340 (06.99) vs 1,773 (05.05)</p>
<p>    Peugeot     1,980 (05.91) vs 2,486 (07.08)</p>
<p>    Honda	 1,235 (03.69) vs 1,328 (03.78)</p>
<p>    Seat	    940 (02.81) vs 1,231 (03.50)</p>
<p>    Toyota	  802 (02.40) vs   676 (01.92)</p>
</text>
